<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the hardened-runtime (notarizable) build.

  Deliberately minimal. Every entitlement here is a restriction lifted off the
  hardened runtime, so each one has to earn its place — and Apple asks about
  the broad ones. This is NOT an App Sandbox build, so the sandbox-only keys
  (network client/server, file access) do not apply and must not be added
  "just in case": they would be inert here and misleading to read.

  Not present, and why:
  - Library validation stays ON. The bundled onnxruntime/sherpa dylibs are
    signed with the same Team ID as the app, so they load without needing
    `disable-library-validation` — which would otherwise let any
    same-architecture dylib into the process.
  - No JIT / unsigned-executable-memory. WebKit runs JavaScript in its own
    process, so the host app never needs them.
  - No DYLD environment variables. The bundle resolves its dylibs through an
    `@executable_path` rpath, not DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH (that is only how
    `cargo run` finds them during development).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Voice dictation records audio through cpal (crates/dictation).

      Under the hardened runtime the `NSMicrophoneUsageDescription` string in
      Info.plist is necessary but NOT sufficient: without this entitlement the
      permission prompt still appears and the user can still grant it, and the
      capture silently returns nothing. The failure looks like a broken feature
      rather than a missing permission, which is what makes it worth stating.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
